# --- The carriers of the two work-orchestration value axes -------------------
ex:cqWorkAxisCarriersShape a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "axis" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ,
        [ logic:columnVariable "term" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsExact .

ex:cqWorkAxisCarriers a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> SELECT ?axis ?term WHERE { VALUES ?axis { gmeow:ContributionKind math:Quantity } ?term rdfs:range ?axis ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> } ORDER BY ?axis ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "Two questions the slice must be able to answer about its own quantitative and attributive surface, asked together because they share a shape. The query is scoped by rdfs:isDefinedBy to the terms this slice OWNS, which is what makes the answer a statement about this vocabulary rather than about every relation in the canon that happens to reach a math:Quantity. Exactly one work-orchestration relation carries the contribution kind, so a record cannot be attributed to a model and an operator at once; and exactly one carries a decision criterion's magnitude into the math: quantity spine, so a criterion's number arrives with its dimension rather than as a bare literal that nobody can convert or compare. A second carrier on either axis would be the drift: two contribution-kind edges make attribution ambiguous, and a second magnitude edge is how an ungrounded number gets back in beside the grounded one."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqWorkAxisCarriersShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqWorkAxisCarriersRowContributionKindcontributionKind , ex:cqWorkAxisCarriersRowQuantitycriterionMagnitude  .

ex:cqWorkAxisCarriersRowContributionKindcontributionKind a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "axis" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:ContributionKind ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:contributionKind ] .
ex:cqWorkAxisCarriersRowQuantitycriterionMagnitude a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "axis" ; gmeow:cellValueIri math:Quantity ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:criterionMagnitude ] .

# --- The relations this slice deliberately leaves untyped at both ends -------
ex:cqUntypedSeamRelationsShape a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "term" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsExact .

ex:cqUntypedSeamRelations a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?term rdfs:domain ?d } FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?term rdfs:range ?r } } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "Leaving both ends of a relation to prose is a real cost — no derived shape can check either side — so the slice should be able to say exactly how often it does so and answer for each case. The answer is one: the rendering seam, which applies to any item carrying authored prose (a guidance item, a note, a dissent, a review rendering) and points into lang:, so declaring a domain would exclude legitimate bearers and declaring a range would duplicate the grounding slice's own typing. Pinning the roster at exactly one entry is what makes the exception stay an exception: a second untyped relation cannot be added without this question failing and the justification being written down."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqUntypedSeamRelationsShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqUntypedSeamRowGuidanceRendering .

ex:cqUntypedSeamRowGuidanceRendering a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:guidanceRendering ] .
